186119750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186348411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186375930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186375937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119750 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186377777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119750 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Curvature Given the Arc Length Parametrization" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119750 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119750 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5c819c5c-aa18-5887-ace3-dfbd9c5700e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120033 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120033 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120033 #edb/ref 1045 "Introduction to Curvature" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120033 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186120580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120033 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120033 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2660cd04-6f2d-5dd7-95c2-55cf96cdbf95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120495 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186119084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120495 #edb/ref 1069 "q-64700" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120495 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120495 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s$, where\n\n$$\nr(s)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩,\\,0\\le s<2\\pi .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120495 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4163ce17-8c2e-5e7a-b5d2-d7191ad32de0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120495 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $T(s)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡s+\\frac{1}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡s+\\frac{1}{2}{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡s+{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120580 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120580 #edb/ref 1061 10650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120580 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "12125b22-92e2-567c-9dc7-87e721cb0430" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120580 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120581 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120581 #edb/ref 1061 10651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120581 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9b2d3984-cd37-5bc8-b3ce-f427ae5bd607" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120581 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120582 #edb/ref 1061 10657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120582 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cd83eef1-8999-5702-814d-b4f011d666e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120582 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120583 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120583 #edb/ref 1061 10658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120583 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a00b3b6-447c-5ccc-97a8-7cd65929b702" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120583 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120594 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120582 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120594 #edb/ref 1061 11099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120594 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d9dd47a2-479b-5929-a71d-4ad46370bfb7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120594 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121002 #edb/ref 1064 "The **curvature** of a curve measures how much the curve \"bends\" at a given point. It can also be thought of as a measure of how much the curve deviates from being a straight line. Curvature is denoted by the Greek letter $\\kappa$ (pronounced \"kappa\"). \n\nIf $\\kappa=0$ at some point on a curve, then that curve looks like a straight line in some neighborhood of the point.\n\nIf the curve $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ is parametrized by the arc length $s,$ then the curvature $\\kappa$ is the magnitude of the change of direction of the unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T$ per unit of arc length. That is,\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) = \\left\\| \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf T}{\\textrm{d}s}  \\right\\|= \\| \\mathbf T'(s) \\|.\n$$\n\nNote that $|| \\mathbf v ||$ denotes the magnitude of the vector $\\mathbf v.$\n\nFor example, suppose we are given the curve \n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(s)= \\left\\langle \\sin\\left(\\dfrac s2\\right), \\: \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2}, \\: -\\cos\\left(\\dfrac s2\\right)\\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \nwhich is parametrized by arc length $s.$ Let's find the curvature of  $\\mathbf r(s)$  at the point where $s={\\pi}.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit tangent vector:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) =\\dfrac 12 \\left\\langle \\cos\\left( \\dfrac s2\\right), \\: \\sqrt{3}, \\: \\sin \\left(\\dfrac s2\\right)\\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we differentiate $\\mathbf{T}(s)$ and evaluate its absolute value at $s=\\pi\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{'}(s) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{s}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{s}{2}))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{s}{2})⟩ \\\\ {T}^{'}(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain the curvature by taking the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =‖{T}^{'}(\\pi )‖=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n**Note:** To calculate $\\kappa,$ the function $\\mathbf{r}(s)$ should be at least twice differentiable with respect to $s.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121002 #edb/ref 1065 2402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121002 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d74577d5-5fe6-5544-bd86-b20fee42defa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121002 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121007 #edb/ref 1064 "If the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ is parametrized by a general parameter $t,$ then\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|}.\n$$\n\nTo understand why this is, remember that the arc length $s$ and the parameter $t$ are related by the formula \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle s(t)= \\int_0^t\\left\\| \\mathbf  r'(x)\\right\\|\\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nBy the chain rule and the fundamental theorem of calculus, then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d  \\mathbf T}{\\textrm d t} = \\dfrac{\\textrm d  \\mathbf T}{\\textrm d s} \\dfrac{\\textrm d  s}{\\textrm d t}= \\dfrac{\\textrm d  \\mathbf T}{\\textrm d s} \\left\\| \\mathbf r'(t)\\right\\|.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}‖ & =‖\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}s}‖‖{r}^{'}(t)‖ \\\\ ‖{T}^{'}(t)‖ & =κ(t)‖{r}^{'}(t)‖ \\\\ κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{'}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{'}(t)‖}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121007 #edb/ref 1065 2484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121007 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a3b41506-4cd1-5589-b3a6-4cd3f4ecbdb2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121007 #edb/ref 1067 "The Curvature of Curves Parametrized Using a General Parameter" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186433633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1045 "Introduction to Curvature" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186433631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433616 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2b8eb350-78af-5600-9e7a-328caccbfa84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433617 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433617 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433617 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1251bed4-415d-5590-a871-e4a9657e13d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433618 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433618 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433618 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1367431b-f708-53d0-907c-401baf44b1b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433619 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433619 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433619 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "481e6b9f-c5af-58b8-b98e-c12965a43b0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433620 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{{(8{t}^{2}+2)}^{3/2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433620 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433620 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5ddff454-cafc-5d0a-8e73-761ad50a723b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433621 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433621 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433621 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ae9b1f32-4af7-5ccc-b6f9-f8acc59e69d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433622 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433622 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433622 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c86e68ce-7275-5906-ac2f-57213bf72bac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433623 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433623 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433623 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d87a76ef-7c66-5822-bbbd-0695f641dc2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433624 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433624 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433624 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e1ed4446-c062-507c-a44a-cf42f43f3e0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433625 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433625 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433625 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e5a5693f-64fa-5920-9519-f34d893234c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433626 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433626 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433626 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f9cd5e7a-fd43-5ce4-9986-155332afc1c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433627 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433627 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433627 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433627 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433627 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433627 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433627 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433627 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433627 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5ef00e22-7033-5539-a4d7-5c70d771c4f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433628 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433628 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433628 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433628 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433628 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433628 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433628 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433628 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433628 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c90f0f81-e6f6-5365-9a31-9800a129aea5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433629 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433629 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80546" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433629 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433629 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433629 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c48a3e25-1a31-5723-bb94-d587dcc4bb55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433629 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${T}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))}^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2 \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+16{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\,2\\,}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433630 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433630 #edb/ref 1069 "q-64696" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433630 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433630 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433630 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d3e668b2-3360-5bad-970e-ebd786d68368" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433630 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $r(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+2t\\,j+1\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}(2t\\,i+2t\\,j+k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}(2\\,i+2\\,j-8t\\,k) \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-8t)^{2}}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8+{8}^{2}{t}^{2}}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8(1+8{t}^{2})}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8}\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{8}\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}})}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433631 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186433632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433631 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "00d70dc7-07a1-5030-82b3-0ddd637fbfb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186433631 #edb